Welsh Assembly Members Don’t Want to “Like Mappies”
There is a dissatisfaction among some members of the National Assembly with a proposal to adopt an abbreviation MWP for their nas (member of the Welsh Parliament).
A problematic solution is connected with the plans to change the name of the Assembly to the Welsh Parliament.
Members of the Assembly from different political parties are concerned about possible jokes with this abbreviation.
One of the Labour, expressing the opinion of his party, expressed concern that the new abbreviation is “rrified Twp and Pwp”.
For our readers not from Welsh: in Welsh twp means "stupid", but pwp - "scaker".
According to a member of the Welsh party, his organization as a whole was “dissatisfied” and offered other options.
representatives of the Conservative party "do not object" against a new abbreviation, but at the same time they note that the MWP is close in spelling the word Muppet (Muppet).
In this Context, the letter w in Wel is pronounced approximately as a letter u in the Yorkshire dialect of English.
The Assembly Committee, which currently elaborates the draft law on the change of name, made the following statement: “The final decision on how the members of the Assembly will be referred to, of course, will remain with them”.
Welsh Managing the Welsh National AssemblY Act of 2017 is mandated to change its name.
In June, the Committee published the results of a public opinion poll about the proposed options, according to which the “Parliament of Welsailles” has found widespread support among the local population instead of “Assembly”.
With regard to the name of the members of the Assembly, the Committee favoured the “Members of the Welsh Parliament Members (WMP), while the MWP option received the greatest public support.
Apparently, the members of the Assembly offer other options, but the Presiding member, Elina Jones, it will be not easy to find a solution that suits everyone. Recall that the draft law on changes should be presented in a few weeks.
Laws on reforms will also include other motivations of the work process of the Assembly, including new rules on the disqualification of the members of the Assembly and the structure of the Committee's system.
The members of the Assembly will vote for the final version of their nasm during the debate on the bill.
The Macedonians will vote in the referendum on the change of the name of their country
On Sunday, the inhabitants of Macedonia will vote on renaming the country to “Republic of North Macedonia”.
The popular vote is designed to resolve a long-standing dispute with neighboring Greece, which has its own province of Macedonia.
The government of Greece has long insisted that the name “Republic of Macedonia” presupposes territorial claims to the Greek province, and has repeatedly spoken out against the accession of its northern neighbour to the European Union and NATO.
Macedonian President Gheorghe Ivanov, an adversarier of the referendum on changing the name, said that he is not going to recognize its results.
However, proponent supporters, including Prime Minister Zoran Zaev, note that changing the country's name is just the price of accession to the EU and NATO.
Crisis in Harlemy parish: the bells of St. Martín froze forever
