What’s the Global Citizen’s Festive and Does It Do Anything to Reduce Poverty?
This Saturday in New York will be held in the Global Citizens (Festival of Citizens of the world), an annual musical event, in which an impressive stellar composition takes part with an equally impressible mission - the end of poverty around the world.
For the seventh year, as part as part of the World's World's Festival, as tens of thousands of people flocked to a large lawn of Central Park, but not only to enjoy performing performers such as Janet Jackson, Cardy B and Sean Ménédes, as well as to talk about a real purpose of the event: eradicating extreme poverty by 2030.
The festival of citizens of the world, which was opened in 2012, is a continuation of a global project to combat poverty, conducted by an international group of human rights defenders hoping to put an end to poverty, increasing the number of people who are actively escaping.
In order to receive a free ticket for the event (if you are not ready to pay for a VIP-ticket), you had to participate in volunteer activities or send an e-mail to a world leader, make a phone call, or perform any other or other significant actions aimed at helping to raise awareness of your goal of ending poverty.
But how successful was the Festival of World Citizens for 12 Years to Achieve?
“Is it the idea of rewarding people’s free attendance attendants to genuinely persuade fellow citizens to demand a call for action, or is this just another case of so-called “clicitivism”, where do people believe that they are making real changes by signing an online petition or sending messages on Twitter?
Contributors of Global Citizen say that more than 19 million “shadowings” have been listed at the festival since 2011, conducted by its supporters who pursue many different goals.
It is noted that thanks to these actions, world leaders have pledged more than $37 billion, which should affect the lives of more than 2.25 billion people by 2030.
In early 2018, the group voiced 3,90 commitments and announcements made as a result of its actions, at least $ 10 billion of which had already been paid or collected.
According to the group estimates, the allocated funds provided immediate assistance to almost 649 million people around the world.
One of the most significant commitments is called The Power of Nutrition: the British Partnership of Investors and Implement Opportunities to “help children fully unleash their potential”, has pledged $35 million to Rwanda to help stop malnutritining in the district. This was done after receiving more than 4,700 tweets from Global Citizens.
“Secured by the UK government, donors, national governments, and Global Citizens like you, we can make a social injustice about malnutrition in history,” Broadcy Ullman, an envoy of Power of Nutrition, said during a live concert in London in April 2018.
The group also stated that after more than 5,000 actions had been taken in urging the United Kingdom to improve food for mothers and children, the Government announced the financing of the Power of the Efficiency Project, which would cover 5 million women and children through activities designed to improve nutrition.
In the response to one of the frequently asked questions on the festival website: “Why do you think that we can put an end to extreme poverty?”
The organizers of the Global citizen answer: “This will be a long and difficult way to stumble and fall from time to time.
But, as in the great movements of the struggle for civil rights and against apartheid, we will achieve a success, because together we are stronger.
