The ingenator of the World Wide web plans to launch a new Internet for Google and Facebook
Tim Berners-Lee, the inventor of the World Wide Web, is launching a startup that claims to be competitive with Facebook, Amazon and Google.
Inrupt’s latest project of a technological legend, Inrupt, is a company based on an open Berners-Lee Solid platform.
Solid allows users to choose where to storequate their data and which people to give access to what kind of information.
Exclusive interview with Fast Company Berners-Lee joked that Inrupt’s goal is to gain “world domination”.
“We have to do it right now,” he says about his startup.
“It’s a historic moment.”
The application uses Solid technology, which allows people to create their own “personal online data stores” or POD.
It can contain lists of contacts, deeds, as well as a caliquary, a music library and other personal and professional tools for working with the data.
The application works on the same principle as Google Drive, Microsoft Outlook, Slack and Spotify - everything can be used in a single browser and at the same time.
The uniqueness of a personal online data stork is that it is completely managed by a user who can access any necessary information.
The company cends this principle “a personal expansion of rights and opportunities by means of data.”
John Bruce, the company’s CEO John Bruce, the idea of Inrupt is that the company has provided resources, processes, and relevant skills to make Solid available to everyone.
Currently, the company includes Berners-Lee, Bruce, the security platform bought by IBM, several full-time developers with whom a contract has been contracted to work on the project, and a community of volunteer programmers.
Beginning of this week, technology developers around the world will be able to create their own decentralized applications using tools available on the Inrupt website.
Burners-Lee said he and his team are not in talks with Facebook and Google about whether his company should make cardinal changes, as a result of which all of their business models will completely change overwhelmed.
"We don't ask for permission."
In his Médium post published on Saturday, Berners-Lee wrote that “Inrupt’s mission – to provide commercial energy and ecosystem to protect the integrity and quality of a new network built on Solid.”
Berners-Lee in 1994 transformed the Internet, creating the World Wide Web conscientific conscientific conscientious form at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.
In recent months, Berners-Lee's voice has sounded quite influential in a debate about neutrality on a network.
Even by launching Inrupt, Berners-Lee will remain the founder and director of the World Wide Web conscientific conscientist, the Internet Foundation and the Open Data Institute.
“I’m incredibly unbelievably optimistic about this next era of the Internet,” Berners-Lee says.
